<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pars</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pars, the region known to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persis">Persis</a> and today the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fars">Fars</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a>. It was the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid dynasty</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardashir-i">Ardashir I</a>, a local ruler of Pars, overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthian-empire">Parthians</a> in 224 CE and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>.</p></div>
